attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `azoR`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, persistent, in a region of plasticity in 4% of calls {S1}. The model names 98% of them, at 0.08 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The rest of the window is fork and variable columns**, 1 to 79, carried by 13 to 86%, in a region of plasticity in 21 to 80% of calls {S2}. Through columns 17 to 22 the `paa` genes run, [[phenylacetic acid degradation]], and columns 72 to 77 carry the `psp` genes, [[phage shock response]] {S2.c17-22, S2.c72-77, Q}. A branch of 14 families runs through columns 5 to 18, `cybB` to `ydcL`, in 12 to 14% {S2.b5}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 98 against 87%, and hesitates less there, 0.08 against 0.64 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 7, is a fork column at 1.26 bits, in a region of plasticity in 73% of calls {H, M}.

@end **The window ends on fork columns.** Column 79, `puuB`, is carried by 41% of chromosomes {S2.c79, E}. The model names 71 to 94% of the stretch, fewest at column 7 {S2}.

@whole **Across the window it names 88% of genes**, 0.63 bits on average, perplexity 1.9 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 0.94 against 0.28 bits, and names fewer genes, 81% against 95% {C}.

